## 1. Executive Summary (Personal)

As a B.Com student at Sri Aurobindo College, Delhi, with a personal interest in retail investing/finance, I realized my Bitcoin research and decision-making could become emotional and unstructured—driven by social media hype, fast-moving narratives, and inconsistent “gut-feel” checks—without a repeatable risk framework.

To solve this, I analyzed **4,175 days** of Bitcoin **OHLC (Open, High, Low, Close)** data covering **2014–2026** and built a structured financial BI workflow using **PostgreSQL, SQL, Power BI, and DAX**. The goal was to convert a long, scattered research process into a repeatable decision-support dashboard built on verified YoY performance and market-cycle context.

**Outcome:** I replaced gut-feeling tracking with a **repeatable YoY-based risk framework** and reduced research time **from weeks to minutes** by using a single dashboard to benchmark years, identify risk triggers, and summarize cycles.

**Business value (who benefits):**

- **Retail investors / Investment Managers:** Get a reliable year-wise growth view to quickly identify which years showed the strongest growth.
- **Risk Analysts / Portfolio Managers:** Use YoY benchmarking plus the **±30% YoY volatility flag** to identify periods of highest risk and compare performance across cycles.
- **Executive Team / Compliance stakeholders:** Consume a clear executive summary and market cycle narrative (4-year cycles observed) for high-level decision-making and risk governance conversations.

---

## 1.5 Why I Built This Project (My Motivation & Learning Journey) 💡

> "If I can analyze a job market like a business problem, why can't I analyze Bitcoin's price history the same way — as a structured risk assessment rather than a prediction?"
> 

### Personal need

- I wanted to stop relying on hype-driven decisions and replace them with a repeatable, explainable framework.
- I needed one structured source that could summarize YoY performance, risk years, and cycle patterns without endless scrolling across charts and posts.

### Analytical project

- I stored the dataset in **PostgreSQL** and used **SQL** with **joins, CTEs, aggregations, window functions (LAG for YoY), and GROUP BY** to compute YoY and summarize patterns.
- I built a **4-page Power BI dashboard** and used **DAX** to implement YoY measures and KPI-level insights for filtering and executive reporting.

### Portfolio case study

- I wrote this BRD as a placement-focused BA case study to demonstrate how I frame a business problem, define requirements, translate them into data work, and deliver executive-ready insights.

### Skills demonstrated (end-to-end BA thinking)

- Business Problem Framing
- Stakeholder Analysis
- Requirements Definition (5 BRs documented)
- Financial Domain Knowledge (OHLC, YoY, market cycles)
- SQL Analysis (YoY, aggregations, window functions)
- Executive Reporting (designed for non-technical executives)
- Data Storytelling (findings framed as business insights)

