## 8. Business Requirements (BR) ✅ (With User Stories + Acceptance Criteria)

**Note:** Requirements are written in BA-friendly format (BR + user story + acceptance criteria) to show how the dashboard supports real investment decisions — not just visuals.

### 8.1 Requirements table

| BR ID | Requirement | User Story | Acceptance Criteria (Specific) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| BR-01 | YoY price performance calculation ✅ Done | As an investment manager, I want to see YoY performance for every year, so that I can compare historical periods at a glance. | Dashboard displays YoY % for every year across all **4,175 days**. |
| BR-02 | Peak and risk year identification ✅ Done | As a risk analyst, I want the strongest and riskiest years clearly identified, so that I can benchmark against historical extremes. | Dashboard explicitly shows **2017 (+605% YoY)** as strongest and **2022 (−41% YoY)** as highest risk. |
| BR-03 | Historical price range analysis ✅ Done | As a portfolio manager, I want the full historical price range visible, so that I can model risk thresholds accurately. | Dashboard shows full price range **$0 to $73,000+** and supports year-based filtering. |
| BR-04 | Interactive filtering by year/period ✅ Done | As an executive, I want to filter by year or period, so that I can focus on specific market cycles without seeing all data at once. | Year/period filtering works across all **4 dashboard pages** without breaking visuals. |
| BR-05 | Executive summary delivery ✅ Done | As an executive team member, I want a plain-language summary page, so that I can understand key findings without interpreting raw data. | Executive Summary page includes **+200% YoY** entry-pattern reference and **−30% YoY** risk-review trigger in plain language. |

### 8.2 Non-functional requirements

- **NFR-01 Performance:** Dashboard remains responsive when filtering across the 4,175-day dataset
- **NFR-02 Usability:** Non-technical executives can interpret findings without training
- **NFR-03 Accuracy:** Power BI YoY results match PostgreSQL query outputs (spot-checked)
- **NFR-04 Maintainability:** SQL queries and DAX measures documented and readable in repository

