## 9. Data Requirements (Technical / Formal)

### 9.1 Data entities

- Daily Price Record (fact) — Date, Open, High, Low, Close, Volume
- Year (dimension) — for YoY aggregation
- Market Cycle (derived grouping) — Cycle 1/2/3
- Risk Flag (derived field) — based on ±30% YoY threshold

### 9.2 Minimum required fields

Date, Open, High, Low, Close, Volume (where available), Derived: Year, YoY % Change, Risk Flag (Yes/No), Market Cycle label

### 9.3 Data transformation rules

- Aggregation of daily OHLC into yearly close-price comparisons for YoY calculation using SQL window function (LAG)
- DAX measure for YoY % change per year
- ±30% threshold rule applied to derive Risk Flag
- Market cycle grouping assigned by year (Cycle 1: 2014–2017, Cycle 2: 2018–2022, Cycle 3: 2023–2026)
- Validation of YoY outputs against manual SQL aggregation queries

---

## 10. Reporting & Visualization Requirements 📊

- KPI cards use consistent formatting (%, year labels, USD price range)
- Risk-flagged years visually distinct (color-coded, e.g., red for high-risk years)
- Key visuals reflect main findings (2017 +605%, 2022 −41%, 4-year cycle pattern)
- DAX measures used for all YoY calculations for consistent filter behavior across pages

---

## 11. Acceptance Criteria ✅

1. Dashboard displays YoY % for every year in the 4,175-day dataset  
2. 2017 (+605% YoY) and 2022 (−41% YoY) clearly identified as benchmark years  
3. Years with YoY beyond ±30% are visually flagged  
4. 4-year market cycle pattern is documented and visible in dashboard  
5. YoY calculations reproducible via SQL validation queries  
6. Executive Summary page includes plain-language recommendation and is accessible via GitHub link  

---

## 12. Risks & Mitigation (What Actually Happened) ⚠️

| Risk/challenge I faced | Why it mattered | What I actually did (mitigation) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Historical patterns may not predict future | Risk of over-reliance on past data | Explicitly stated as disclaimer in executive summary page |
| YoY alone oversimplifies volatility | Single metric hides intra-year swings | Supplemented with ±30% threshold rule and 4-year cycle context |
| Data validation across SQL and Power BI | KPI mismatches undermine credibility | Spot-checked Power BI YoY outputs against manual SQL queries |

---

